{"title":"The hyper-NIMBY of earlier Cape Town and South Africa","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/950692073/0/marginalrevolution~The-hyperNIMBY-of-earlier-Cape-Town-and-South-Africa.html","date":1773684917000,"content":"<blockquote><p>The most controversial of the forced removals occurred in the second half of the 1960s, with the expulsion of 65,000 coloureds from District Six, a vibrant inner-city ward of Cape Town, where whites, many of the slumlords, owned 56% of the property.  Against their will, District Six residents were moved out to the sandy townships of the Cape Flats.  In Johannesburg, the inner-city suburb of Sophiatown, where blacks could own freehold property, was another notorious site of forced removals.  Often long-established community institutions such as churches and schools had to be abandoned.</p></blockquote>\r\n<p>That is from the very good book by Hermann Giliomee <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Afrikaners-Concise-History-Hermann-Giliomee-ebook/dp/B08NV5NTHF/ref=sr_1_1?crid=110INZ49KPFY9&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.aWODkhrqNJvKmTnwhd_BVMFK3M7mN9x4Jua9KZfxwvVwSJHDh1xayW88GdIILnXzNOXPaHO0Xu2FrdI2J4jj5xpZHabr3TqzlFtekc0s857ziwFkK73s8I-vQGTBPJz6M1kmR6qHb2225TadfVQtWHcVqQXCGrwCMfCrXvlaBLBw-H-6peVsjd7B3Gjr2XL3EhOo4xbL3Hehwt-m8vpYvbk55SEVM-RtWlKMazVZI4M.5Bx6yBHCFS8KjQVxXbnQIHnj8OysMJWABEpds9Hd7nA&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=The+Afrikaners%3A+A+Concise+History&amp;qid=1773519561&amp;sprefix=%2Caps%2C1217&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">The Afrikaners: A Concise History</a>.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/03/the-hyper-nimby-of-earlier-cape-town-and-south-africa.html\">The hyper-NIMBY of earlier Cape Town and South Africa</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" w